<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Shell: Help</title>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_head.html.erb' %>
  </head>
  <body class="site-page help-page">
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_navigation.html.erb' %>
    <main id="main" class="page-container help-content">
      <header class="help-header">
        <h1>Shell: Help</h1>
        <p class="section-intro">A little help for your channel's command line.</p>
      </header>
      <section id="get-started" class="help-section" aria-labelledby="start-title">
        <h2 id="start-title">Get started</h2>
        <ol class="getting-started-steps">
          <li><%= partial 'public/partials/_install_button.html.erb' %> and authorize Shell for your workspace.</li>
          <li>Invite <code>@sh</code> into a Slack channel.</li>
          <li>Type <code>man</code> to see the commands, or <code>ls</code> to list files.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Each channel has its own rudimentary file system. This is a shell bot inside Slack, not a connection to your computer's shell.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="help-section" aria-labelledby="commands-title">
        <h2 id="commands-title">Commands &amp; questions</h2>
        <details id="is-this-a-joke" class="help-topic" open>
          <summary>Is this a joke?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Also, it works! Shell is a tiny Unix-like shell inside Slack, because apparently Slack needed a command line. Its commands and per-channel file system really work, but it is a toy, not a remote terminal.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Command reference</summary>
          <pre><%= CGI.escapeHTML(SlackShellbot::Commands::Man::HELP) %></pre>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>How do I create and read a file?</summary>
          <p>Try <code>touch notes</code> to create a file, <code>ls</code> to see it, and <code>cat notes</code> to read its contents. Use <code>mkdir projects</code> to create a directory.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>How do I leave the editor?</summary>
          <p>The basic <code>vi</code>-like editor updates messages in place. Use <code>:wq</code> to quit and save, or <code>:q</code> to quit without saving.</p>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section id="support" class="help-section" aria-labelledby="support-title">
        <h2 id="support-title">Need a hand?</h2>
        <p>Contact <a href="mailto:dblock@vestris.com">dblock@vestris.com</a>, DM <a href="https://twitter.com/playplayio">@playplayio</a>, or <a href="https://github.com/slack-ruby/slack-shellbot/issues">report an issue on GitHub</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_footer.html.erb' %>
  </body>
</html>
